
**v1.0** Initial release
**v1.1** 'Edit' tab for changing location, size & transparency
**v1.2** Options to edit time and network interface
**v1.2 - v2.4** Unknown changes by teejee2008
**v2.5** Transition to fork for 'conky-manager2' adding conky 1.10 support and Dutch translation.
**v2.6** Portuguese-Brazil added, default nvidia theme fix, support for import on non-ConkyManagerTheme archive.
**v2.7** Fix 'Edit Widget' now includes network interface replacement for conky 'if_up' and 'addr' variables.
**v2.72** French and German translations, lua detection additions, meson vscode and small fixes.
**v2.73** Korean translation, debian packaging updates, add quality icon artwork.
**v3.2.0** Check for Updates: the app checks GitHub for new releases at startup (can be turned off) and from the menu, shows release notes, downloads the matching .deb or tarball, verifies its SHA-256 checksum, installs it with your password and restarts into the new version. curl is now a dependency.
**v3.1.0** Redesigned interface in the style of CleanMyLinux: sidebar navigation with Overview, Widgets, Themes, Add Widgets and Settings pages; preview gallery with on/off switches, search and pack filters; drag-and-drop import; live CPU, memory and running-widget meters; restyled dialogs and a new icon. Bundles two new widget packs in place of the old default themes: Liquid Glass (glass panels) and Minimal (the same widgets drawn on the wallpaper, plus four top-middle clocks, with text color that follows the wallpaper). Edit Position and Look now only writes the settings you change; wallpaper "zoom" and "tiled" scaling fixed for Cinnamon/GNOME/MATE; conky and gsettings output no longer floods the terminal; simpler About window.
**v3.0.1** The .deb now requires conky, 7-Zip and ImageMagick instead of only recommending them; the missing-tools notice shows the apt command to install them.
**v3.0.0** Conky Manager 3 (renamed package: conky-manager3).
**v2.74** Reliability fixes: exact running-widget detection via /proc (stopping one widget no longer kills others whose path shares a prefix; paths with spaces work), preview-generation timer no longer re-kills widgets every 10s, no GTK calls from worker threads, Lua (1.10+) configs now get missing settings inserted and keep value case/quoting, theme import no longer drops a stray "nul" file into ~/.conky, missing tools are a warning instead of a hard exit, 7z/7zz accepted in place of 7za, desktop detected from XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP (adds MATE/Budgie), GNOME dark-mode wallpaper set too, freedesktop icon names instead of deprecated GTK stock items.
